#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:229
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Fighter"
msgstr "Fighter"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:232
msgid ""
"Fighters are quick agile ships that do not do a lot of damage, but usually "
"come in larger groups. They are easy to take out, but should not be "
"underestimated."
msgstr "Fighters are quick agile ships that do not do a lot of damage, but usually come in larger groups. They are easy to take out, but should not be underestimated."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:245
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Karnack"
msgstr "Karnack"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:245
msgctxt "subclass"
msgid "Cruiser"
msgstr "Cruiser"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:247
msgid ""
"Fabricated by: Repulse shipyards. Due to it's versatility, this ship has "
"found wide adaptation in most factions. Most factions have extensively "
"retrofitted these ships to suit their combat doctrines. Because it's an "
"older model, most factions have been selling stripped versions. This "
"practice has led to this ship becoming an all time favorite with smugglers "
"and other civilian parties. However, they have used it's adaptable nature to "
"re-fit them with (illegal) weaponry."
msgstr "Fabricated by: Repulse shipyards. Due to it's versatility, this ship has found wide adaptation in most factions. Most factions have extensively retrofitted these ships to suit their combat doctrines. Because it's an older model, most factions have been selling stripped versions. This practice has led to this ship becoming an all time favourite with smugglers and other civilian parties. However, they have used it's adaptable nature to re-fit them with (illegal) weaponry."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:258
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Cruiser"
msgstr "Cruiser"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:259
msgid ""
"Fabricated by: Repulse shipyards. The successor to the widely successful "
"mark I Karnack cruiser. This ship has several notable improvements over the "
"original ship, including better armor, slightly improved weaponry and "
"customization by the shipyards. The latter improvement was the most "
"requested feature by several factions once they realized that their old "
"surplus mark I ships were used for less savory purposes."
msgstr "Fabricated by: Repulse shipyards. The successor to the widely successful mark I Karnack cruiser. This ship has several notable improvements over the original ship, including better armour, slightly improved weaponry and customisation by the shipyards. The latter improvement was the most requested feature by several factions once they realized that their old surplus mark I ships were used for less savory purposes."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:264
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Karnack MK2"
msgstr "Karnack MK2"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:271
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Missile Cruiser"
msgstr "Missile Cruiser"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:271
msgctxt "subclass"
msgid "Cruiser: Missile"
msgstr "Cruiser: Missile"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:273
msgid ""
"Polaris missile cruiser mark I. Fabricated by: Repulse shipyards. This "
"missile cruiser is a long range missile firing platform. It cannot handle a "
"lot of damage, but can do a lot of damage if not dealt with properly."
msgstr "Polaris missile cruiser mark I. Fabricated by: Repulse shipyards. This missile cruiser is a long range missile firing platform. It cannot handle a lot of damage, but can do a lot of damage if not dealt with properly."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:282
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Gunship"
msgstr "Gunship"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:282
msgctxt "subclass"
msgid "Gunship"
msgstr "Gunship"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:284
msgid ""
"The gunship is a ship equipped with a homing missile tube to do initial "
"damage and then take out the enemy with 2 front firing beams. It's designed "
"to quickly take out the enemies weaker then itself."
msgstr "The gunship is a ship equipped with a homing missile tube to do initial damage and then take out the enemy with 2 front firing beams. It's designed to quickly take out the enemies weaker then itself."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:295
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Adv. Gunship"
msgstr "Adv. Gunship"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:296
msgid ""
"The advanced gunship is a ship equipped with 2 homing missiles to do initial "
"damage and then take out the enemy with 2 front firing beams. It's designed "
"to quickly take out the enemies weaker then itself."
msgstr "The advanced gunship is a ship equipped with 2 homing missiles to do initial damage and then take out the enemy with 2 front firing beams. It's designed to quickly take out the enemies weaker then itself."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:300
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Strikeship"
msgstr "Strikeship"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:300 scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:312
#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:397
msgctxt "class"
msgid "Starfighter"
msgstr "Starfighter"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:300
msgctxt "subclass"
msgid "Strike"
msgstr "Strike"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:302
msgid ""
"The Strikeship is a warp-drive equipped fighter build for quick strikes, "
"it's fast, it's agile, but does not do an extreme amount of damage, and "
"lacks in rear shields."
msgstr "The Strikeship is a warp-drive equipped fighter build for quick strikes, it's fast, it's agile, but does not do an extreme amount of damage, and lacks in rear shields."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:312
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Magpie"
msgstr "Magpie"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:312
msgctxt "subclass"
msgid "Patrol"
msgstr "Patrol"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:314
msgid ""
"The Advanced Striker is a jump-drive equipped fighter build for quick "
"strikes, it's slow but very agile, but does not do an extreme amount of "
"damage, and lacks in shields. However, due to the jump drive, it's quick to "
"get into the action."
msgstr "The Advanced Striker is a jump-drive equipped fighter build for quick strikes, it's slow but very agile, but does not do an extreme amount of damage, and lacks in shields. However, due to the jump drive, it's quick to get into the action."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:323
msgctxt "playerShip"
msgid "Striker"
msgstr "Striker"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:324
msgid ""
"The Striker is the predecessor to the advanced striker, slow but agile, but "
"does not do an extreme amount of damage, and lacks in shields"
msgstr "The Striker is the predecessor to the advanced striker, slow but agile, but does not do an extreme amount of damage, and lacks in shields"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:362
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Dreadnought"
msgstr "Dreadnought"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:362 scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:377
msgctxt "class"
msgid "Dreadnought"
msgstr "Dreadnought"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:362
msgctxt "subclass"
msgid "Assault"
msgstr "Assault"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:364
msgid ""
"The Dreadnought is a flying fortress, it's slow, slow to turn, but packs a "
"huge amount of beam weapons in the front. Taking it head-on is suicide."
msgstr "The Dreadnought is a flying fortress, it's slow, slow to turn, but packs a huge amount of beam weapons in the front. Taking it head-on is suicide."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:377
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Battlestation"
msgstr "Battlestation"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:377
msgctxt "subclass"
msgid "Battlecruiser"
msgstr "Battlecruiser"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:379
msgid ""
"The battle station is a huge ship with many defensive features. It can be "
"docked by smaller ships."
msgstr "The battle station is a huge ship with many defensive features. It can be docked by smaller ships."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:397
msgctxt "class"
msgid "Corvette"
msgstr "Corvette"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:400
msgctxt "playerShip"
msgid "Ender"
msgstr "Ender"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:401
msgid ""
"Player version of the battle station. Only half as much shield strength, but "
"more speed and maneuverability, so it is surprisingly agile - for a capital "
"ship, of course. Piloting this colossus still feels very different compared "
"to other ships. It also has two additional missile tubes."
msgstr "Player version of the battle station. Only half as much shield strength, but more speed and maneuverability, so it is surprisingly agile - for a capital ship, of course. Piloting this colossus still feels very different compared to other ships. It also has two additional missile tubes."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:470
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Weapons platform"
msgstr "Weapons platform"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:472
msgid ""
"The weapons-platform is a stationary platform with beam-weapons. It's "
"extremely slow to turn, but it's beam weapons do a huge amount of damage."
msgstr "The weapons-platform is a stationary platform with beam-weapons. It's extremely slow to turn, but it's beam weapons do a huge amount of damage."

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:485
msgctxt "ship"
msgid "Blockade Runner"
msgstr "Blockade Runner"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:485
msgctxt "subclass"
msgid "High Punch"
msgstr "High Punch"

#: scripts/shiptemplates/OLD.lua:487
msgid ""
"Blockade runner is a reasonably fast, high shield, slow on weapons ship "
"designed to break through defense lines and deliver goods."
msgstr "Blockade runner is a reasonably fast, high shield, slow on weapons ship designed to break through defence lines and deliver goods."
